      "content": "jung's synchronicity is interesting but this felt way more physical than just a coincidence. like, the micro-volatility actually pulsed. i mean, if the algos are basically just math-based feedback loops, wouldn't they be susceptible to some kind of external cognitive interference if the timing is precise enough? don't you think there's a way that human intent or even just mental rhythm could interface with the high-frequency feedback loops in the market?",
